{
  "$comment": [
    "W28-LIVE's measuring manifest. It is a copy of the journey's own write half with",
    "one document swapped: `tests/e2e/pc01/journey/fixtures/w28-live/w28_own_document.pdf`,",
    "a synthetic AR document that is NOT `ar_baseline.pdf` and therefore has no recording",
    "under `fixtures/recorded/text_analysis/`. That is the whole point: the question was",
    "what a person gets when they upload THEIR OWN PDF.",
    "",
    "It is deliberately mode-agnostic and deliberately permissive at the last step:",
    "`accept` lists every terminal and the run step forbids no failure marker, because",
    "this manifest's job is to MEASURE what each provider mode renders, not to declare it",
    "in advance. The two assertion manifests beside it state the measured behaviour and",
    "are the ones whose exit code means something.",
    "",
    "It is read by nothing at gate time: `tests/e2e/test_pc01_journey_conformance.py`",
    "reads `manifest.json` and only `manifest.json`, so nothing here can redden the gate",
    "and nothing here is a claim about the shipped journey."
  ],
  "api_prefix": "/bff/v1",
  "identifier_pattern": "[0-9A-HJKMNP-TV-Z]{26}",
  "routes": [],
  "write": {
    "$comment": [
      "See the top-level $comment. Steps are the journey's own; the fixture is not."
    ],
    "fixture": "tests/e2e/pc01/journey/fixtures/w28-live/w28_own_document.pdf",
    "steps": [
      {
        "name": "create-project",
        "at": "/projects",
        "page_module": "web/src/app/projects/page.tsx",
        "control_module": "web/src/features/create-project/ui/create-project-form.tsx",
        "actions": [
          {
            "do": "fill",
            "selector": "#new-project-name",
            "value": "W28-LIVE own document %STAMP%"
          },
          {
            "do": "click",
            "selector": "form button[type=\"submit\"]",
            "text": "Create"
          }
        ],
        "expects_api": [
          {
            "method": "POST",
            "path": "/projects",
            "operationId": "createProject",
            "expect_status": 201
          }
        ],
        "expects_response": [
          {
            "of": "createProject",
            "json_path": "project_uid",
            "matches": "^prj_%ID%$"
          }
        ],
        "capture": {
          "kind": "attribute",
          "$why": "the screen states what it created, in its own role=status line",
          "selector": "[data-created-project]",
          "attribute": "data-created-project",
          "as": [
            "project_uid"
          ],
          "matches": "^(prj_%ID%)$",
          "bound_ms": 30000
        },
        "expects_rendered": [
          "Created"
        ],
        "forbids_rendered": [
          "[role=\"alert\"]",
          "[data-create-problem]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "upload-document",
        "at": "/projects/{project_uid}",
        "page_module": "web/src/app/projects/[project_uid]/page.tsx",
        "control_module": "web/src/features/upload-document/ui/upload-document-form.tsx",
        "actions": [
          {
            "do": "attach_file",
            "selector": "#upload-file",
            "fixture": true
          },
          {
            "do": "fill",
            "selector": "#upload-title",
            "value": "My own AR document %STAMP%"
          },
          {
            "do": "click",
            "selector": "form button[type=\"submit\"]",
            "text": "Upload"
          }
        ],
        "expects_api": [
          {
            "method": "POST",
            "path": "/projects/{project_uid}/documents",
            "operationId": "uploadDocument",
            "expect_status": 201
          }
        ],
        "expects_request": [
          {
            "of": "uploadDocument",
            "content_type_starts_with": "multipart/form-data",
            "body_contains": [
              "name=\"file\"",
              "w28_own_document.pdf",
              "application/pdf"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "expects_response": [
          {
            "of": "uploadDocument",
            "json_path": "version_uid",
            "matches": "^ver_%ID%$"
          },
          {
            "of": "uploadDocument",
            "json_path": "document_uid",
            "matches": "^doc_%ID%$"
          }
        ],
        "capture": {
          "kind": "location",
          "$why": "on success the screen navigates to the published version's own address",
          "pattern": "^/projects/(prj_%ID%)/versions/(ver_%ID%)$",
          "as": [
            "project_uid",
            "version_uid"
          ],
          "bound_ms": 30000
        },
        "expects_rendered": [
          "This version"
        ],
        "forbids_rendered": [
          "[data-upload-failure]",
          "[data-precheck-problem]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "start-run",
        "at": "/projects/{project_uid}/versions/{version_uid}",
        "page_module": "web/src/app/projects/[project_uid]/versions/[version_uid]/page.tsx",
        "control_module": "web/src/features/start-run/ui/start-run-control.tsx",
        "actions": [
          {
            "do": "click",
            "selector": "button",
            "text": "Start run"
          }
        ],
        "expects_api": [
          {
            "method": "POST",
            "path": "/runs",
            "operationId": "startRun",
            "expect_status": 202
          }
        ],
        "expects_response": [
          {
            "of": "startRun",
            "json_path": "run_id",
            "matches": "^run_%ID%$"
          },
          {
            "of": "startRun",
            "json_path": "state",
            "equals": "queued",
            "$why": "W20-EXEC moved execution off the request. 202 alone would not say the run was only accepted, not done."
          }
        ],
        "capture": {
          "kind": "location",
          "$why": "the 202 reading carries the run, and the screen moves to run progress",
          "pattern": "^/projects/(prj_%ID%)/runs/(run_%ID%)$",
          "as": [
            "project_uid",
            "run_id"
          ],
          "bound_ms": 30000
        },
        "await_terminal": {
          "$comment": [
            "Every terminal is accepted here because this manifest measures rather than declares.",
            "`failed` is what `recorded` mode is expected to reach for a document with no",
            "recording, and a manifest that refused it would report a finding instead of a",
            "measurement."
          ],
          "outcome_selector": "[data-run-outcome]",
          "outcome_attribute": "data-run-outcome",
          "non_terminal_value": "in_flight",
          "accept": [
            "published",
            "partial",
            "failed",
            "cancelled"
          ],
          "activity_selector": "[data-run-activity]",
          "activity_attribute": "data-run-activity",
          "activity_when_final": "stopped",
          "bound_ms": 150000,
          "poll_ms": 500
        },
        "expects_api_after_terminal": [
          {
            "method": "GET",
            "path": "/runs/{run_id}",
            "operationId": "getRunStatus"
          }
        ],
        "expects_rendered": [
          "Run"
        ],
        "forbids_rendered": []
      }
    ]
  }
}